  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nCall or Text Us: (310) 954-9449\n\nRequest An Appointment\n\nPatient Registration\n\nHome\n\nAbout Us\n\nOur Team\n\nDr. Jonathan Shadi\n\nDr. Saman Vahedi\n\nOur Technology\n\nCone Beam 3D Imaging\n\nProcedures\n\nOral Surgery\n\nBone Grafting\n\nPre-Prosthetic Surgery\n\nPlatelet Rich Fibrin (PRF)\n\nOral Pathology\n\nOrthognathic (Corrective Jaw) Surgery\n\nDental Implants\n\nRestorative Dentistry\n\nFull Mouth Reconstruction\n\nImpacted Canines\n\nWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nFacial Trauma Fractures\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nPatient Center\n\nPatient Information\n\nInsurance & Finance\n\nAreas We Serve\n\nMar Vista\n\nPalms\n\nCulver City\n\nWestwood\n\nSawtelle\n\nCentury City\n\nBrentwood\n\nSanta Monica\n\nWest Los Angeles\n\nSurgical Instructions\n\nBefore Anesthesia\n\nOral Surgery Pre-Operative Instructions\n\nPost-Operative Instructions\n\nReferring Doctors\n\nBlogs\n\nContact Us\n\n\n# About Us\n\n\n\n## About Wilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center\n\n\nChoosing an oral surgeon is one of the more consequential healthcare decisions you can make. Whether you need a wisdom tooth removed, a dental implant placed, or a more complex surgical procedure, the training, technology, and environment your surgeon provides will shape every part of that experience. At Wilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center, our surgeons and staff have built a practice in West Los Angeles that meets that standard at every level: board-level credentials, advanced in-office technology, and the kind of personalized attention that makes a real difference when you are facing oral surgery.\n\nWe serve patients from across the Westside, including Beverly Hills, Santa Monica, Brentwood, Culver City, Westwood, and the surrounding communities. Our office at 12300 Wilshire Blvd #326, Los Angeles, CA 90025 offers a modern, comfortable surgical environment where you can receive the full scope of oral and maxillofacial care without being referred across town for imaging, anesthesia, or additional procedures.\n\n\n## Our Surgeons\n\n\nWilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center is led by two board-certified oral and maxillofacial surgeons. You can read their full biographies on our Meet Us page, but here is a brief overview of the training that backs every procedure we perform.\n\nDr. Jonathan R. Shadi, DDS\n\nOral & Maxillofacial Surgeon\n\nB.S. Neuroscience, UCLA (College Honors)\n\nDDS, USC School of Dentistry (Dean’s List)\n\nJohn Ingle Research Award, 2009\n\nOMFS Internship, Veterans’ Affairs Hospital, Long Beach\n\nOMFS Residency, UCSF–Fresno, 2014\n\nView Dr. Shadi’s Bio →\n\nDr. Saman Vahedi, DDS\n\nB.S. Molecular, Cell & Developmental Biology, UCLA\n\nDDS, Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry, USC\n\nOMFS Residency, University of Nebraska Medical Center\n\nChief Resident, 2013–2014\n\nDiplomate, American Board of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgeons\n\nView Dr. Vahedi’s Bio →\n\nBoard-certified oral and maxillofacial surgeons complete four to six years of hospital-based residency training after dental school, rotating through anesthesiology, general surgery, internal medicine, and other disciplines. The American Board of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery requires candidates to pass written and oral examinations reviewed by a panel of peers before certification is granted. This level of training distinguishes oral and maxillofacial surgeons from general dental providers, particularly for cases that involve bone loss, anatomical complexity, sedation, or multiple procedures in a single visit.\n\n\n## What We Offer\n\n\nOur practice provides the full scope of oral and maxillofacial surgery under one roof, eliminating the need for multiple specialist referrals across the Westside. Our surgeons and staff are trained and equipped to handle:\n\nSingle implants, multiple implant cases, and full-arch restoration\n\nLearn More →\n\nSurgical extractions including impacted and complex cases\n\nRidge augmentation and bone volume restoration for implant readiness\n\nIV Sedation & Anesthesia\n\nAdministered in-office by our board-certified surgeons\n\nOn-site for same-visit surgical planning, no outside referrals\n\nComprehensive rehabilitation and pre-prosthetic surgery\n\nOrthognathic Surgery\n\nCorrective jaw procedures for function and alignment\n\nSurgical exposure and treatment of impacted teeth\n\nFacial Trauma & Fractures\n\nEmergency and reconstructive care for facial injuries\n\nOral Pathology & Biopsies\n\nEvaluation and tissue biopsy for oral lesions and abnormalities\n\nPRF & Growth Factors\n\nPlatelet-Rich Fibrin therapy to support healing and recovery\n\nEvery treatment plan is built around your specific anatomy, goals, and timeline. We take the time to walk you through your options, explain what each procedure involves, and answer your questions before any clinical decision is made.\n\n\n## Our Technology and Facility\n\n\nOur office at 12300 Wilshire Blvd #326 in West Los Angeles is equipped with the diagnostic and surgical technology that modern oral surgery requires.\n\n3D Cone Beam CT\n\nOn-site imaging for precise, same-visit surgical planning with no outside referrals or delays.\n\nIn-Office Anesthesia\n\nIV sedation and general anesthesia administered by the same board-certified surgeons performing your procedure.\n\nModern Surgical Suite\n\nA comfortable, purpose-built environment with hospital-level monitoring standards in a private West LA office.\n\nOur Location →\n\nIV sedation and general anesthesia are administered by Dr. Shadi and Dr. Vahedi themselves, using the same monitoring standards applied in hospital operating rooms. Patients who prefer to be sedated for their procedure, or whose cases require it, can undergo treatment in the same familiar office environment without the cost and complexity of a hospital or ambulatory surgery center visit.\n\n\n## Serving the West Los Angeles Community\n\n\nWilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center has been part of the West Los Angeles community since our founding. Patients come to us from Beverly Hills, Santa Monica, Brentwood, Westwood, Century City, Sawtelle, Mar Vista, Culver City, and the surrounding areas, drawn by the combination of board-certified surgical credentials, advanced technology, and individualized care that is difficult to find in a single practice.\n\nWhether you were referred by your general dentist, found us while researching your options, or are returning for additional treatment, we are glad you are here. Our team is committed to making every visit informative, comfortable, and productive, so you leave with a clear understanding of your oral health and a path forward that makes sense for your situation. You can also read what our patients say on our reviews page.\n\nReady to Schedule Your Consultation?\n\nOur board-certified surgeons at Wilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center are here to answer your questions and build a plan that fits your needs.\n\nRequest an Appointment or call (310) 846-8978\n\n\n## Schedule a Consultation\n\n\nIf you are ready to discuss your oral surgery needs with a board-certified surgeon, we invite you to request an appointment online or reach us through our contact page. Our team is available to answer questions, explain your options, and help you take the next step with confidence. You can also review our patient resources, including pre-operative and post-operative instructions, before your visit.\n\n\n### Contact Information\n\n\n12300 Wilshire Blvd #326 Los Angeles, CA 90025\n\n(310) 954-9449\n\n\n### Hours of Operation\n\n\nMonday\n\n8:00am – 4:00pm\n\nTuesday\n\nWednesday\n\nThursday\n\nFriday\n\nSaturday\n\nClosed\n\nSunday\n\n© 2026 Wilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center. All Rights Reserved.\n\nAccessibility Statement\n\nMEET US\n\nSurgical Instructio...\n\nBlog\n\nMeet Us\n\nPatient Registration Form\n\nPre-prosthetic Surgery\n\nOral Surgery Pre-operative Instructions\n\nIV Sedation / General Anesthesia\n\nPost-operative Instructions",
